      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T12:38:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we validate the pool size before storing it? The API accepts a `u32 n_addr`, but `nat_alloc_pool_t::num` is `u16`. With exactly 65,536 addresses, `pool-\u003enum` becomes zero and this modulo divides by zero; larger values wrap and use only part of the configured pool. Rejecting counts above `UINT16_MAX` (or widening `num`) would avoid this.",
      "revId": "8149a8cc1384121ca91e0661e72623842ab8fc4b",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
