      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T08:22:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Heads-up for a follow-up: deleting an allocation pool does not free its `remaining` vector before `pool_put_index()`, so repeated add/delete operations on pools larger than 13 addresses leak memory. This predates this change and is not blocking here, but larger pools becoming usable makes it more relevant.",
      "revId": "8149a8cc1384121ca91e0661e72623842ab8fc4b",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
